    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "686ca443_1d85074d",
        "filename": "test/stm32f_rtc.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T23:36:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There could be a race condition here. The load could end up requiring several assembly instructions, which would leave an opportunity for the interrupt to fire in the middle and modify the counter, which would result in reading a corrupted value ([more details](https://concurrencyfreaks.blogspot.com/2013/08/interrupt-handler-in-c11-with-atomics.html)). It would be safer to make `interrupt_counter` an `atomic_t` and use `atomic_get()` to get the value and `atomic_add()` to increment it in the interrupt handler (similar to the `stm32f_rtc.c` file).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 28,
        "endChar": 50
      },
